{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-160431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{v}^{2}+uv \\\\ v-u\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\ncompute the value of the Jacobian determinant at the point where $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/state.json" "file_sha256" "b19b634dcfeb749b9451489a660a3fe56b6601a09e826160ec23868a7d6ad209"} {"question" "q-160431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)={v}^{2}+uv$ and $y(u,v)=v-u.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =v & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =2v+u \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =-1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}v & 2v+u \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =v\\cdot 1-(2v+u)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =v+2v+u \\\\  & =3v+u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, when $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],$ the value of our Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n{\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(8,-2)}=3(-2)+8=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/state.json" "file_sha256" "b19b634dcfeb749b9451489a660a3fe56b6601a09e826160ec23868a7d6ad209"} {"question" "q-160431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "43cab90a72588be0455fd213c0fdb9dd28356f8d17115f9193aec6c1ad9ec193"} {"question" "q-160431" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/state.json" "file_sha256" "b19b634dcfeb749b9451489a660a3fe56b6601a09e826160ec23868a7d6ad209"} {"question" "q-160431" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/state.json" "file_sha256" "b19b634dcfeb749b9451489a660a3fe56b6601a09e826160ec23868a7d6ad209"} {"question" "q-160431" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/state.json" "file_sha256" "b19b634dcfeb749b9451489a660a3fe56b6601a09e826160ec23868a7d6ad209"} {"question" "q-161832" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(1,5)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(uv) \\\\ u{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/state.json" "file_sha256" "b19b634dcfeb749b9451489a660a3fe56b6601a09e826160ec23868a7d6ad209"} {"question" "q-161832" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))≈|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\cdot {{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{⏟}}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{u} & \\frac{1}{v} \\\\ {v}^{2} & 2uv\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot 2uv-\\frac{1}{v}\\cdot {v}^{2} \\\\  & =2v-v \\\\  & =v \\\\ {\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(1,5)} & =v\\,{|}_{u=1\\,v=5} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & ≈|5|\\cdot \\delta A \\\\  & =5\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/state.json" "file_sha256" "b19b634dcfeb749b9451489a660a3fe56b6601a09e826160ec23868a7d6ad209"} {"question" "q-161832" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "43cab90a72588be0455fd213c0fdb9dd28356f8d17115f9193aec6c1ad9ec193"} {"question" "q-161832" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/state.json" "file_sha256" "b19b634dcfeb749b9451489a660a3fe56b6601a09e826160ec23868a7d6ad209"} {"question" "q-161832" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "11\\,\\delta A"] ["math" "3\\,\\delta A"] ["math" "5\\,\\delta A"] ["math" "8\\,\\delta A"] ["math" "\\delta A"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/state.json" "file_sha256" "b19b634dcfeb749b9451489a660a3fe56b6601a09e826160ec23868a7d6ad209"} {"question" "q-161832" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5\\,\\delta A"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/state.json" "file_sha256" "b19b634dcfeb749b9451489a660a3fe56b6601a09e826160ec23868a7d6ad209"} {"question" "q-161841" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u+v} \\\\ -uv\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-preserving?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/state.json" "file_sha256" "b19b634dcfeb749b9451489a660a3fe56b6601a09e826160ec23868a7d6ad209"} {"question" "q-161841" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving at the points where the Jacobian determinant is positive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}>0.\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u+v} \\\\ -uv\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u+v} & {e}^{u+v} \\\\ -v & -u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={e}^{u+v}\\cdot (-u)-(-v)\\cdot {e}^{u+v} \\\\  & ={e}^{u+v}(v-u).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u+v}(v-u) & >0 \\\\ v-u & >0 \\\\ v & >u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNotice that the equation \n\n$$\nv=u\n$$\n\ndefines a straight line, and the coordinates of, say, $(2,3)$ satisfy the inequality. \n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving must be the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/assets/8bec16b8ed5083071e21761e6b2e649e136ce0662f7e5ab764161491094c0609.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/state.json" "file_sha256" "b19b634dcfeb749b9451489a660a3fe56b6601a09e826160ec23868a7d6ad209"} {"question" "q-161841" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "43cab90a72588be0455fd213c0fdb9dd28356f8d17115f9193aec6c1ad9ec193"} {"question" "q-161841" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/state.json" "file_sha256" "b19b634dcfeb749b9451489a660a3fe56b6601a09e826160ec23868a7d6ad209"} {"question" "q-161841" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/assets/0b764651dbc7999e7af13214685796b5045fab89f101bbc72bf413112df3c51f.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/assets/8bec16b8ed5083071e21761e6b2e649e136ce0662f7e5ab764161491094c0609.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/assets/c244350524a52123e2e97db4cd8eb4f57737b8b15746eb72a8d54eac32a4f3cf.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/assets/fd2a51ca3a1654c2e857018268bf251366472a2c5d7f90009d5ccfbf1b1edd9d.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/assets/fe7bb422a3f992ea88a900e63b2c55df99bce3a785929901c248abadfadf23f1.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/state.json" "file_sha256" "b19b634dcfeb749b9451489a660a3fe56b6601a09e826160ec23868a7d6ad209"} {"question" "q-161841" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/assets/8bec16b8ed5083071e21761e6b2e649e136ce0662f7e5ab764161491094c0609.png"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/state.json" "file_sha256" "b19b634dcfeb749b9451489a660a3fe56b6601a09e826160ec23868a7d6ad209"} {"question" "q-161842" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} \\\\ u-\\frac{1}{3}v\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-reversing?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/state.json" "file_sha256" "b19b634dcfeb749b9451489a660a3fe56b6601a09e826160ec23868a7d6ad209"} {"question" "q-161842" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing at the points where the Jacobian determinant is negative:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}<0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} \\\\ u-\\frac{1}{3}v\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3{u}^{2} & -v \\\\ 1 & -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3{u}^{2})\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3})-(1)\\cdot (-v) \\\\  & =v-{u}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v-{u}^{2} & <0 \\\\ v & <{u}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNotice that the equation \n\n$$\nv={u}^{2}\n$$\n\ndefines a parabola, and the coordinates of, say, $(1,-1)$ satisfy the inequality. \n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing must be the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/assets/1368ee41963c1abcc320d2cd35449c08599582f37c7d68f750e137fcdcd2e57b.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/state.json" "file_sha256" "b19b634dcfeb749b9451489a660a3fe56b6601a09e826160ec23868a7d6ad209"} {"question" "q-161842" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "43cab90a72588be0455fd213c0fdb9dd28356f8d17115f9193aec6c1ad9ec193"} {"question" "q-161842" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/state.json" "file_sha256" "b19b634dcfeb749b9451489a660a3fe56b6601a09e826160ec23868a7d6ad209"} {"question" "q-161842" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/assets/1368ee41963c1abcc320d2cd35449c08599582f37c7d68f750e137fcdcd2e57b.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/assets/3033f0ae73e3f484fc5d3d65e388062feba1824fb3da9971d560cf2f518f49bb.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/assets/cb5b22ff46569b231d122c2ed11bd412907f36271a033d86769435adf9fe48c7.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/assets/d477a9f312fc2fb0a5a4c2d13164c96118aa70b53cf23db80be9ec698151e6fd.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/assets/fe7bb422a3f992ea88a900e63b2c55df99bce3a785929901c248abadfadf23f1.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/state.json" "file_sha256" "b19b634dcfeb749b9451489a660a3fe56b6601a09e826160ec23868a7d6ad209"} {"question" "q-161842" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/assets/1368ee41963c1abcc320d2cd35449c08599582f37c7d68f750e137fcdcd2e57b.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/state.json" "file_sha256" "b19b634dcfeb749b9451489a660a3fe56b6601a09e826160ec23868a7d6ad209"} {"question" "q-161875" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(0,3)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u-{v}^{2} \\\\ u+v\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/state.json" "file_sha256" "b19b634dcfeb749b9451489a660a3fe56b6601a09e826160ec23868a7d6ad209"} {"question" "q-161875" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))≈|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\cdot {{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{⏟}}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u & -2v \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u)\\cdot 1-1\\cdot (-2v) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u+2v \\\\ {\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(0,3)} & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u+2v)\\,{|}_{u=0\\,v=3} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+2(3) \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & ≈|6|\\cdot \\delta A \\\\  & =6\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/state.json" "file_sha256" "b19b634dcfeb749b9451489a660a3fe56b6601a09e826160ec23868a7d6ad209"} {"question" "q-161875" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "43cab90a72588be0455fd213c0fdb9dd28356f8d17115f9193aec6c1ad9ec193"} {"question" "q-161875" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/state.json" "file_sha256" "b19b634dcfeb749b9451489a660a3fe56b6601a09e826160ec23868a7d6ad209"} {"question" "q-161875" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12\\,\\delta A"] ["math" "16\\,\\delta A"] ["math" "3\\,\\delta A"] ["math" "6\\,\\delta A"] ["math" "9\\,\\delta A"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/state.json" "file_sha256" "b19b634dcfeb749b9451489a660a3fe56b6601a09e826160ec23868a7d6ad209"} {"question" "q-161875" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6\\,\\delta A"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052618/state.json" "file_sha256" "b19b634dcfeb749b9451489a660a3fe56b6601a09e826160ec23868a7d6ad209"}] "usage" {"q-161832" []} "basis" 1769 "retractions" [[17592186129462 :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(1, 5)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $δA$. Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T$, given by\n\n$T: \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}\\ln (uv) \\\\ uv^{2}\\end{bmatrix}$?"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186126579 17592186126580 17592186126581 17592186126582 17592186126583] "immutable_fields" [[17592186126578 :answer-field/correct] [17592186126578 :answer-field/id] [17592186126578 :answer-field/key] [17592186126578 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
